{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem of finding how many different combinations of $5 bills and $2 bills can be used to make a total of $17, we can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[5x + 2y = 17\\]\n\nwhere \\(x\\) is the number of $5 bills and \\(y\\) is the number of $2 bills. We need to find all non-negative integer solutions to this equation.\n\nLet's solve for \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[2y = 17 - 5x\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{17 - 5x}{2}\\]\n\nFor \\(y\\) to be an integer, \\(17 - 5x\\) must be even. Since 17 is odd, \\(5x\\) must be odd, which means \\(x\\) must be odd. So, \\(x\\) can be 0, 1, 3, or 5 (since \\(5 \\times 5 = 25\\) which is greater than 17).\n\n","prefix_end":621,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,315,9271,1246,1657,2155,27459,315,400,20,18610,323,400,17,18610,646,387,1483,311,1281,264,2790,315,400,16,22,11,582,646,738,705,279,2701,23606,1447,78045,20,87,488,220,17,88,284,220,16,22,59,2533,2870,17767,87,57758,374,279,1372,315,400,20,18610,323,17767,88,57758,374,279,1372,315,400,17,18610,13,1205,1184,311,1477,678,2477,60935,7546,9904,311,419,23606,382,10061,594,11625,369,17767,88,57758,304,3793,315,17767,87,59,7731,78045,17,88,284,220,16,22,481,220,20,87,59,921,78045,88,284,1124,37018,90,16,22,481,220,20,87,15170,17,11035,2533,2461,17767,88,57758,311,387,458,7546,11,17767,16,22,481,220,20,87,57758,1969,387,1496,13,8704,220,16,22,374,10322,11,17767,20,87,57758,1969,387,10322,11,892,3363,17767,87,57758,1969,387,10322,13,2055,11,17767,87,57758,646,387,220,15,11,220,16,11,220,18,11,476,220,20,320,11284,17767,20,1124,15136,220,20,284,220,17,20,57758,892,374,7046,1091,220,16,22,3593,10061,594,1779,1817,3204,897,315,17767,87,59,7731,16,13,1416,17767,87,284,220,15,59,982,256,1124,58,88,284,1124,37018,90,16,22,481,220,20,1124,50853,220,15,15170,17,92,284,1124,37018,90,16,22,15170,17,92,284,220